\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{Yes. A read-only MCP server (\code{mcp/}) over the built forest and the Lean environment, run locally by agents and humans, rebuilt in CI. Tools (MVP):}
  \ul{
    \li{\code{search(query, k, filter)}: hybrid lexical + embedding search over node bodies (generated and handwritten), docstrings, decision text; filters by taxon/status/area;}
    \li{\code{get(address)}: full node;}
    \li{\code{neighbors(address, direction)}: dependencies / dependents / cited decisions;}
    \li{\code{open_tasks(area, kind)}: \code{stated}/\code{sorry} nodes, sorted by unblocked-dependents;}
    \li{\code{decision(id)} and \code{acceptance(id)}: registry lookups with status;}
    \li{\code{type_search(pattern)}: Loogle-style search over the environment for the project's namespaces.}
  }
  \p{No write tools; changes go through PRs. Index sources: \code{build/forest/} plus the handwritten \code{forest/}. The server is a thin wrapper; the forest is the index.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{An agent that cannot find the decision node will re-derive the decision, usually differently. Retrieval at task time is how frozen decisions actually bind. Grepping thirteen million lines is not a plan.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{frozen (MVP tool list provisional).}
}
